{"answer": "The main difference is that **precision** checks how many of your predictions were actually correct, while **recall** checks how many of the actual positives you managed to find. Precision is TP / (TP + FP) and recall is TP / (TP + FN) [p.1].

Think of a spam filter. If it labels 100 emails as spam and only 10 are real spam, its precision is 10/100 = 0.1 because most of its guesses were wrong. If there were actually 20 real spam emails in your inbox, its recall is 10/20 = 0.5 because it missed half of them.

